cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, cite the release you used by tag and commit; main moves."
title: "Subject-Rooted Governance: an executable research artifact for governing long-lived AI actors as persistent subjects"
type: software
authors:
  - name: TRANTOR LABS
    address: Singapore
repository-code: https://github.com/TrantorLabs/subject-rooted-governance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
abstract: >-
  Companion artifact of "Persistent Subjecthood and Responsibility Black Holes: A Subject-Rooted
  Governance Architecture for Long-Lived AI Actors". A Rust reference harness with independent
  checkers for the paper's structural conditions G1-G6 and target properties O1-O3, twenty
  fault-injection scenarios across four baselines, a four-valued responsibility-black-hole
  adjudicator, a bounded finite-world explorer reproducing the P1-P3 counterexamples, two TLA+
  models executed with SANY/TLC, and a contract-level adapter for SoulAuth v0.3.0 authentication
  facts. Results are deterministic and regenerated in CI from the committed source.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI agents
  - accountability
  - provenance
  - authorization
  - formal methods
  - Rust
